The signal peaks when a short token completes the stem, rather than on
whole-word tokens. Related vest/vel/vozh/vez forms are included. Word-initial
water spellings and long words respond less. A vowel-initial suffix retains
part of the response for one token. The Japanese guiding character 導 is a
second, smaller trigger. This is a surface-spelling approximation, not a
complete semantic classifier.
