"""A local calculation-language detector, not a mathematical evaluator.

Computing/calculating words and explicit formulas get positive responses.
Their word-piece continuations are often stronger than whole-word tokens.
The prepositions in 'expression for', 'calculation of', and 'value of'
are separate signals, as are 'come up with' and 'look up'.  A short text
suffix joins split words; it is cleared at document boundaries.
